  "blocks": [
    {
      "t": "p",
      "x": "Not every improvement needs a full gut renovation. For many Winnipeg offices, shops, clinics and multi-unit buildings, a handful of small commercial renovation ideas can change how customers, tenants and staff feel about a space, usually with less cost and disruption."
    },
    {
      "t": "p",
      "x": "Here are ten projects that can deliver real impact for the effort."
    },
    {
      "t": "h2",
      "x": "Front of house"
    },
    {
      "t": "p",
      "x": "**1. Refresh the entrance.** A new entry door, better lighting and clean signage are the first things people see. In Winnipeg, a well-sealed door can also cut drafts and heating costs."
    },
    {
      "t": "p",
      "x": "Downtown? The [Storefront Success grant](https://news.gov.mb.ca/news/index.html?item=74757&posted=2026-08-11), announced in August 2026, may help eligible retailers, restaurants and cafés in its program area with entrances, signage and lighting, while funding lasts. The release's remaining application deadlines are December 31, 2026 and March 31, 2027. Bridgeland Builders has no role in the program. Our [commercial renovation financing guide](/blog/how-to-finance-a-commercial-renovation-without-breaking-the-bank) has the details."
    },
    {
      "t": "p",
      "x": "**2. Paint.** A fresh, consistent colour scheme updates a space without touching the layout. Choose durable, washable finishes for high-traffic areas."
    },
    {
      "t": "p",
      "x": "**3. Replace worn flooring in high-traffic zones.** Entries, corridors and reception areas show wear first. [Commercial-grade vinyl plank or carpet tile](/services/flooring) can be installed in sections, often after hours."
    },
    {
      "t": "p",
      "x": "**4. Upgrade the lighting.** Swapping old fluorescent fixtures for LED improves how the space looks, lowers energy use and reduces maintenance."
    },
    {
      "t": "h2",
      "x": "Comfort and function"
    },
    {
      "t": "p",
      "x": "**5. Modernize washrooms.** New fixtures, touchless faucets, partitions and lighting make an older washroom feel new. Customers notice."
    },
    {
      "t": "p",
      "x": "**6. Add a meeting room or quiet room.** A few new walls and a door can turn unused open space into the room your team keeps asking for."
    },
    {
      "t": "p",
      "x": "**7. Refresh the staff kitchen or break room.** New counters, a sink, cabinets and better lighting can lift morale."
    },
    {
      "t": "p",
      "x": "**8. Improve accessibility.** Lever handles, accessible washroom upgrades, ramps or power door operators open your space to more customers and can help meet code."
    },
    {
      "t": "h2",
      "x": "Building envelope and exterior"
    },
    {
      "t": "p",
      "x": "**9. Replace failing windows or doors.** Foggy windows and drafty doors make a building look tired and can drive up heating bills through a Winnipeg winter. See [window and door replacement](/services/windows-and-doors)."
    },
    {
      "t": "p",
      "x": "**10. Repair masonry and exterior paint.** Cracked brick, failing mortar and peeling paint hurt curb appeal and can let water in. See [masonry and stucco repair](/services/masonry-stucco) and [exterior painting](/services/exterior-painting)."
    },
    {
      "t": "p",
      "x": "A crack that keeps widening can be a structural question for an engineer, so have the cause checked first. Exterior work waits for the warmer months, and paint needs late spring to early fall."
    },
    {
      "t": "h2",
      "x": "How to make small renovations go smoothly"
    },
    {
      "t": "li",
      "x": "**Phase the work** so your business stays open."
    },
    {
      "t": "li",
      "x": "**Schedule after hours or weekends** for customer-facing areas. [Within 150 metres of a home](https://www.winnipeg.ca/building-development/property-records/construction-your-neighbourhood), the City allows loud work only from 7 a.m. to 9 p.m. on weekdays and 9 a.m. to 9 p.m. on weekends and holidays."
    },
    {
      "t": "li",
      "x": "**Check permits.** Even small commercial renovations can need a permit. Cosmetic work such as paint and flooring [generally doesn't](https://legacy.winnipeg.ca/ppd/Documents/Permits/CommercialAlterationDesignSummary/Guide-Commercial-Alteration-Design-Summary.pdf), but the City says to [get one before starting any alteration to any part of a building](https://www.winnipeg.ca/building-development/building-renovating/inspections/commercial/building)."
    },
    {
      "t": "li",
      "x": "**Test before you disturb.** In older buildings, have suspect materials such as old tile and adhesive tested first; see [asbestos testing before renovating](/blog/asbestos-testing-before-renovating-manitoba)."
    },
    {
      "t": "li",
      "x": "**Bundle projects.** Doing several small jobs in one visit can save on mobilization costs."
    },
    {
      "t": "h2",
      "x": "Where to start with small commercial renovations"
    },
    {
      "t": "p",
      "x": "Walk through your space as a first-time customer or tenant would. Note the first five things that look worn, dated or uncomfortable. Those are your priorities."
    },
    {
      "t": "h2",
      "x": "The bottom line"
    },
    {
      "t": "p",
      "x": "Small commercial renovations can improve how a space looks and works without closing your doors. Start with what people see and touch every day."
    },
    {
      "t": "p",
      "x": "**Planning small upgrades?** In Winnipeg and nearby communities, Bridgeland Builders can scope just the part you need, from entrances and flooring to washrooms and windows, with evening and weekend scheduling where it helps. [**Book a Free On-Site Visit**](/book-online)."
    },
    {
      "t": "p",
      "x": "**Related reading:** [Commercial renovations](/services/commercial-renovations) · [Commercial interior design: function and looks](/blog/how-to-balance-functionality-and-aesthetics-in-a-commercial-space) · [12 Upgrades That Reduce Commercial Building Operating Costs](/blog/reduce-commercial-building-operating-costs)"
    }
  ],
